From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 19:37:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: skip AP_VLAN in the link reconfig of a restart

An AP_VLAN of an MLD AP holds the links of its AP. A hardware
restart therefore passes the VLAN to the driver op for a link
change. mac80211 never adds an AP_VLAN to the driver, so the op
fails its in-driver check with a warning.

A hardware restart skips an AP_VLAN in the link reconfig, as it does
when it adds interfaces to the driver. The VLAN needs no driver call,
because it takes its links and its channel context from its AP.

Fixes: 90233b0ad215 ("wifi: mac80211: Create separate links for VLAN interfaces")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/mac80211/util.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -2074,6 +2074,10 @@ int ieee80211_reconfig(struct ieee80211_
 		if (!ieee80211_sdata_running(sdata))
 			continue;
 
+		/* an AP_VLAN is never in the driver; its links follow its AP */
+		if (sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN)
+			continue;
+
 		if (ieee80211_vif_is_mld(&sdata->vif)) {
 			struct ieee80211_bss_conf *old[IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS] = {
 				[0] = &sdata->vif.bss_conf,
